<article class="env-corollary" id="B75892">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B75892">Corollary <span data-tag="B75892">6.2.3.12</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be a semitopos containing a diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { &amp;  Y \ar [dr]^{g} &amp;  \\ X \ar [ur]^{f} \ar [rr]^{h} &amp;  &amp;  Z} \]
</div>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
If $f$ and $g$ are effective epimorphisms, then so is $h$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
If $h$ is an effective epimorphism, then so is $g$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/5C64D1" data-tag="5C64D1">6.2.3.10</a>, and the observation that we have an equality $f^{\ast } \circ g^{\ast } = h^{\ast }$ of functions $\Sub (Z) \rightarrow \Sub (X)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>